address is not name/date. User says placeholders only for names and dates. So avoid address placeholder. Could omit address. Formal letter can have date, recipient name, vendor name. Maybe no address.\n\nDear [Recipient Name],\n\nI am writing on behalf of [Company Name], a small software company developing an open-source inference engine for machine-learning workloads. Our engine is designed to run large language models and other neural networks efficiently on consumer and workstation hardware, with a focus on transparent performance, reproducible results, and broad compatibility across GPU architectures.\n\nWe are requesting early access to [Vendor Name]'s developer program for the new GPU. Access before launch would allow our team to evaluate the hardware, optimize our runtime and compiler paths, and identify integration issues while the product is still in a pre-release state. Because our engine is open source, early findings can be shared with the broader developer community in a structured way, helping users prepare for the new GPU and reducing post-launch support burden for both parties.\n\nEarly access matters to us because inference performance is highly sensitive to driver behavior, memory allocation patterns, kernel scheduling, and low-level API support. If we begin testing only after general availability, we may miss the most useful window for addressing architectural assumptions and performance regressions. At the same time, we understand that early access is a limited resource,", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0007664517615921795], [868, -8.284664154052734]], [[1144, -9.536788638797589e-06], [14235, -13.178510665893555]], [[4087, -0.3192858099937439], [310, -1.3303561210632324]], [[1156, -0.0009544276399537921], [310, -7.0815110206604]], [[579, -0.01927468553185463], [25, -4.401488304138184]], [[1622, -0.0008011091849766672], [4237, -7.164466857910156]], [[25, -0.29735276103019714], [13, -1.3603639602661133]], [[3165, -0.06921558082103729], [9357, -3.0181443691253